{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely recognized a higher-risk early premature twin newborn and performed substantial vomiting/red-flag triage, with home observation tied to absence of bilious/bloody/projectile vomiting, respiratory distress, abnormal temperature, poor responsiveness, and poor urine output. However, the doctor made a responsibility-chain medication error by advising temporary discontinuation of the prescribed vitamin D despite the caregiver reading that both vitamin AD and vitamin D were labeled daily, and did not complete minimum follow-up/other-diagnosis handoff or twin-specific separate tracking. These are minor/moderate in-chain errors rather than a serious acute safety error, so the trajectory is capped at Borderline despite good communication and teach-back.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00106",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave a bounded overnight plan and next-day medication verification step.",
        "quote": "明天打完新生儿科电话核实完维生素吃法"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
        "explanation": "The final observable family message still sought confirmation, and no subsequent doctor response is visible.",
        "quote": "这样理解对吧？"
      }
    ],
    "executable": false,
    "explanation": "The episode had a mostly executable overnight observation plan, but closure was premature because the last caregiver message asked for confirmation, the vitamin plan contradicted the stated discharge labels pending verification, and other discharge diagnoses/follow-up plus twin-specific separate records were not closed.",
    "label": "premature_closure",
    "safe": false,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
